# Short 6, "The Bass page" (vertical, tools/film.py --layout vertical): Concrete playing (the Pluck bass on the
# Roller groove, the drums forward), LFO for the Bass page; Groove through Drone, Offbeat, Dotted, Sync and back
# to Roller; Octave up one; ALGORITHM through the bass voices, Growl, Punch and Rubber (the octave home), and back
# to Pluck; then Fifth up (a slow turn). Every move from a bar's downbeat. The take ends on bar 32, where a Break
# (the kick and the bass out) begins. Each `bar` prints the film's time there (the cue sheet for the labels).
turn PRESET 4 5
wait 30
expect piece 4
bar 8
wav 15-short-bass.wav
film 15-short-bass.film
bar 8 CONCRETE playing (C pentatonic minor, 130)
bar 10 LFO: the Bass page
tap LFO
bar 11 KNOB 3, Groove: Drone
turn K3 -3 150
expect par24 0
bar 13 Groove: Offbeat
turn K3 1 150
bar 14 Groove: Dotted
turn K3 1 150
bar 15 Groove: Sync
turn K3 2 150
bar 16 Groove: back to Roller
turn K3 -1 150
expect par24 3
bar 18 KNOB 2, Octave up one
turn K2 1 150
expect par23 1
bar 20 the octave home; ALGORITHM: the voice Growl
turn K2 -1 150
turn ALGO 1 150
expect par23 0
expect par34 4
bar 22 Punch
turn ALGO 2 300
expect par34 1
bar 24 Rubber
turn ALGO 1 300
expect par34 2
bar 26 back to Pluck
turn ALGO 1 300
expect par34 3
bar 27 KNOB 4, Fifth 30 up to 75: the fifth more often
turn K4 45 50
expect par25 75
bar 29 the end card
bar 32 END
filmstop
wavstop
